# OPERATIONS §2.3 (M3): with a base that loads, the refused scenarios' lines first, then the asks refused alone, then
# the warnings load decides. bad is refused (LOAD-DUP, its q is the base's); q_low names lowered, whose file isn't
# given (LOAD-SCENARIO, refused alone); qx, in bad's world, is covered by bad's line; spare is read by nothing
# (WARN-UNREAD, L §8.5). Exit 1: the first line isn't `ok`.
=== options check exit=1
=== m.tally
model f
  tally 2
  on 2025-01-01
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31
source s "synthetic"
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
input spare: int
ask q: minor(DUK)
ask q_low: minor(DUK) in lowered
=== bad.tally
scenario bad over f
  tally 2
  from 2025-01-01
def q: int = 1
ask qx: q in bad
=== expect
scenario bad: refused: LOAD-DUP q is declared twice (bad.tally:4)
q_low: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO ask q_low names lowered, neither the model nor a loaded scenario (m.tally:10)
warning: WARN-UNREAD input spare is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD source s is read by nothing
